//
//  Nodes 1, stage 3a: the town replicator's payload (protocol/repl/node_layout.h) against the 18 payloads the retail server sent
//  (tests/capture_node_layout.h, generated by tools/capture/gen_node_layout.py: the first open of each node, level and season in 15 captures; the spike
//  research/spike_replicator decoded them to their last bit).
//
//    * the schema: the generated ANodeLayoutReplicator has the fast array with the header and the seven-member item
//    * the 18 retail payloads read to their last bit, typed (the leading bit, the header, the counters and the items), and the typed payload written again is the EXACT
//      bits of the capture; each is 481 + 800 x items bits plus the tags' 320
//    * the header: no tag, two tags, the refusals (an empty tag, 64 tags, a non-ASCII tag); a truncated header does not read
//    * the server's side: the first sync of a replicator's array is IDs 1..N and ArrayReplicationKey N and the field writes the retail payload's bits; the same sync again
//      changes nothing and sends a connection that has it nothing; a level change is one delta (the old items deleted, the new added, the header and PlotChangeVersion new)
//      that a client applying it ends up equal to the server with; a header-only change reaches the client too
// ============================================================================
